From 3fc472cd807cf9df0ca39dfdfb6df40d5f29b8dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sijie52 <sijie5452@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:07:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(c): add C language analysis with CAnalyzer and C taint
 checker

Wire @ant-yasa/uast-parser-c (local file: link like the Python parser)
into the parser registry, worker, starter and packaging, and add:

- CAnalyzer: external linkage for non-static functions and file-scope
  variables across files, extern declarations, header static inline
  functions, pointer aliasing (`&x`, `*p = v`, live `*p` reads), struct
  and array aggregates with nested writes, do-while and single-pass
  loops, unreachable code after return/break/goto, constant if
  conditions, labels, sizeof as a constant, numeric conversion as an
  injection barrier, and a per-entrypoint time budget
  (entryPointTimeoutQuickMs) checked at call boundaries
- C library model writing taint back into output buffers, including the
  wide-character variants (strcpy, strcat, memcpy, sprintf, snprintf,
  sscanf, realpath, wcsncat, swprintf, ...)
- taint_flow_c_input checker and taint-flow-c-default pack: call-graph
  roots as entrypoints, main argv/envp and rule-config sources, buffers
  written by source functions through casts and pointer arithmetic
- rule_config_c.json: command injection (POSIX and Windows CRT), format
  string (narrow and wide), buffer overflow, path traversal and SQL
  injection sinks. Variadic sinks use "*" because rule args only accept
  single indexes
- engine regression test `npm run test-c`
